Participants
One hundred and eighty-two students enrolled at a large southeastern US university voluntarily participated in this study. The sample consisted of 74% Caucasians, 15% African Americans, 3% Asians, 2% Hispanics, 1% Native Americans, and 5% of participants who self-identified as “other”. Approximately 66% of the participants were female, and the mean age was 20.2 (SD = 3.2). Participants indicated that they spent an average of 9.0 h on the Internet per week (SD = 7.6).
